---
code: K0006
title: Bad Directive
severity: ERROR
since: 0.1.0
category: parse
deprecated: False
tags: [ parse, syntax, directive ]
description: "'@' directive token is not followed by a valid directive name"
---

The `@` character introduces a directive, so it must be immediately followed by a valid directive identifier (such as `@state`, `@view`, `@update`, or `@use`).

## Example

This error occurs when `@` is followed by whitespace, punctuation, a number, or the end of the file:

```kura
@ state {
  count: Int = 0
}
```

It also occurs if `@` is used on its own without a name:

```kura
@
view {
  Text("Hello")
}
```

## Solution

Remove any whitespace between `@` and the directive name, and ensure the name is a valid identifier:

```kura
@state {
  count: Int = 0
}
```

If you intended to include a literal `@` character inside text content, place it inside a string literal instead:

```kura
Text("contact@example.com")
```
